        <article class="min-w-0 flex-1 space-y-16 pb-24 text-[15px] leading-7 text-gray-700">

            <header>
                <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Documentation</p>
                <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900">How Windcraft works</h1>
                <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-gray-600">The gallery, projects, the editor and agents, step by step. If a word looks unfamiliar, check the <a href="#glossary" class="font-medium text-gray-900 underline">glossary</a> at the bottom.</p>
            </header>

            <section id="what" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">What is Windcraft?</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">Windcraft has two doors. The <strong class="text-gray-900">gallery</strong> is where you come to look at designs and choose one. The <strong class="text-gray-900">editor</strong> is where you make a design, with its code beside it. Every design lives in a <strong class="text-gray-900">project</strong>.</p>
                <p class="mt-3">It is for developers who want code to copy, designers who want to work visually, teams who want one look across a product, and anyone building with an AI coding tool. It is free.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="start" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Quick start</h2>
                <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Open the <a href="/" class="font-medium underline">gallery</a>, pick a category, and look at a design. Press <em>Code</em> to see it, and the copy button to take it. No account needed.</li><li>Press <strong class="text-gray-900">Open in editor</strong> to make your own copy, or <strong class="text-gray-900">Save</strong> to keep it. Both ask which project it goes in.</li><li>Or press <strong class="text-gray-900">New design</strong> in the top bar: a dialog opens with the code on the left and the design on the right. Write or paste code, press Save, and choose its project. (On the Projects page the top bar has <strong class="text-gray-900">New project</strong>, which makes a project and opens the editor on a blank page with the code panel below it.)</li><li>Set the project's look (colours, font, corners) on its page, then turn <strong class="text-gray-900">Public</strong> on for any design you want to share in the gallery.</li></ol>
            </section>

            <section id="gallery" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">The gallery</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">The gallery is organised by category.</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Preview and Code</strong>: switch between how a design looks and its code. Pick a phone size, light or dark, or full screen.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Copy</strong>: copy the code. You need no account for this.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Save</strong>: put a private copy into one of your projects.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Open in editor</strong>: make your own copy in a project and open it.</li></ul>
            </section>

            <section id="projects" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Projects</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">A project is where everything starts: a design cannot exist outside one. It is a folder for your pages and components, with one shared look, a share link, and a place to export from.</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">New project</strong> (top bar) creates it at once and opens the editor on a blank page. Rename it on its page.</li><li>The <strong class="text-gray-900">Projects</strong> page lists your projects as cards, each with the categories of the designs in it. Search by name or tag in the top bar, tick one or more categories in the <em>All Categories</em> dropdown, and press tag chips below to narrow further. A project shows when it matches any ticked category and any chosen tag.</li><li>The project page shows a board of every page and component. Drag frames to arrange them. Two tabs list them as <strong class="text-gray-900">Pages</strong> and <strong class="text-gray-900">Components</strong>: a design's category decides which (the Pages category group are pages, every other category is a component).</li><li>Select an item to open its details: set its <strong class="text-gray-900">category</strong> and <strong class="text-gray-900">tags</strong>, turn <strong class="text-gray-900">Public</strong> on or off, <strong class="text-gray-900">export</strong> it, see its <strong class="text-gray-900">history</strong> and restore a version, <strong class="text-gray-900">move</strong> it to another project, tick <strong class="text-gray-900">Use as AI reference</strong>, or <strong class="text-gray-900">delete</strong> it. Search, a category filter and tag chips narrow the list.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Import</strong> adds designs from HTML files, a zip, or pasted HTML. Long pages can be split into sections.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Design guide</strong> (Projects page) downloads a markdown summary of your designs, for a CLAUDE.md or an agent.</li><li>Deleting a project deletes everything in it.</li></ul>
            </section>

            <section id="editor" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">The editor</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">The editor shows the design and its code side by side. Edit either: change the code and the design follows, drag or restyle on the canvas and the code follows.</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Tools</strong>: select, hand, interact (try the page as it will run), frame, shapes, text, and an add menu.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Code panel</strong>: syntax colours, auto-closing tags, find and replace, Tailwind class suggestions, and <strong class="text-gray-900">Format</strong> to tidy it. It sits below the design by default; the dock button moves it to the left, and your choice is remembered.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Properties</strong>: edit an element's spacing, size, type, colour, border and effects. Each value is written to where it comes from (a Tailwind class or CSS).</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Save</strong> opens a small form under the toolbar: name, category (which decides page or component), project, description, tags, and visibility. A new project's first save asks only for a name.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">New design</strong> in the gallery's top bar opens the same editor in a dialog, with a button to open it in the full editor.</li></ul>
            </section>

            <section id="theme" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">A project's look</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">On the project page, the <strong class="text-gray-900">Theme</strong> tab holds four choices that the editor, every preview and your exports use:</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Brand colour</strong>: one colour. Its eleven shades become <code>brand-50</code> to <code>brand-950</code>, and the colour itself is <code>brand-600</code>.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Gray</strong>: which of Tailwind's five grays <code>gray-*</code> means here.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Font</strong>: a Google Fonts family, or the system font.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Corners</strong>: how round <code>rounded-*</code> is.</li></ul>
                <p class="mt-3">Change it once and every page and component in the project follows.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="share" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Publishing and sharing</h2>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Public</h3>
                <p class="mt-3">Designs are private. Turn <strong class="text-gray-900">Public</strong> on for a design on its project page and it appears in the gallery, under its category, where anyone can look at it and copy the code.</p>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Share link</h3>
                <p class="mt-3">The <strong class="text-gray-900">Share</strong> button on a project page makes a link. Anyone who opens it can look at the whole project in its theme and copy the code, with no account. Nothing in it can be changed. <strong class="text-gray-900">Stop sharing</strong> ends the link.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="export" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Export and history</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">Any design can be copied or exported as HTML, React, Vue or Svelte, and as a design spec or a profile. The page code stays plain HTML with Tailwind, so you are never locked in.</p>
                <p class="mt-3">To keep the project's look in exported code, take the theme setup too: it is a small Tailwind config for the brand colour, gray, font and corners.</p>
                <p class="mt-3">Every change keeps the earlier version. Open an item's <em>History</em> to see them and restore one.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="agents" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Connect your tools</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">The <a href="/connect" class="font-medium underline">Connect</a> page (in the sidebar, signed in) lets AI tools read and write your projects, instead of guessing. Pick your tool there and follow its short guide. All of it is optional.</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Claude on the web</strong>: add Windcraft as a custom connector in claude.ai, paste the address shown on the page, and allow access. No token is needed. A <em>Run test</em> button checks the connection.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Claude Code</strong>: put your access token in an environment variable, then run <code>claude mcp add</code> with the command on the page. A downloadable kit adds a project config and a <code>CLAUDE.md</code> section.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Cursor and other MCP clients</strong>: use the server address and an <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> header with your token.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Figma plugin</strong>: sign in with your account once, then send a design into a project as editable code.</li><li><strong class="text-gray-900">Claude Design</strong>: download a pack of your design guide and the designs marked <em>Use as AI reference</em>, and attach it there.</li></ul>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Access token</h3>
                <p class="mt-3">Claude Code, Cursor and other MCP clients sign in with an access token, kept in its own box on the Connect page. It is shown once when you create it; you can regenerate it or revoke it, and either stops the old one at once. <strong class="text-gray-900">Treat it like a password</strong>: anyone who has it can read and add to your projects. Keep it in an environment variable or your tool's secret settings, never in a file you share. The <em>Connected</em> list on the page shows the apps and Figma sign-ins with access, each with a Disconnect button.</p>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">What the agent can do</h3>
                <div class="mt-3 divide-y divide-gray-200 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white text-sm"><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">get_design_guide</code><span>A summary of your designs: colours, fonts, spacing and an index. Agents read it first.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">get_context</code><span>Which account and active project the agent is working in.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">list_projects, get_project, create_project, update_project, set_active_project</code><span>See, create and change projects (name, description, brief), and choose the one saves go to.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">search_components</code><span>Find designs by keyword or tag.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">get_component</code><span>Get one design as HTML, React, Vue or Svelte.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">get_design_spec</code><span>Look at a design as a labelled tree of elements.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">apply_design_patch</code><span>Make small changes to a design by element id.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">save_component, save_design, save_pages</code><span>Save a component, a finished page, or several pages. Every save goes into a project: name one, or set an active project.</span></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-3 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr]"><code class="font-mono text-gray-900">list_tags</code><span>List your tags.</span></div></div>
            </section>

            <section id="glossary" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Glossary</h2>
                <dl class="mt-4 divide-y divide-gray-200 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white text-sm"><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Gallery</dt><dd>Public designs, by category, most liked first.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Project</dt><dd>Where designs live: a folder with a shared look, a share link and exports.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Page and component</dt><dd>A page is a whole screen; a component is a smaller part. Both live in a project.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Theme</dt><dd>A project's brand colour, gray, font and corners.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Public</dt><dd>A design turned on for the gallery. Private by default.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Share link</dt><dd>A view-only link to a whole project.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">MCP</dt><dd>The standard that lets coding tools use your projects.</dd></div><div class="grid gap-1 p-4 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr]"><dt class="font-medium text-gray-900">Access token</dt><dd>A secret that lets a tool like Claude Code use your projects. Claude on the web and the Figma plugin sign in instead.</dd></div></dl>
                <p class="mt-6 text-sm">Still stuck? See <a href="/support" class="font-medium underline">Support</a>.</p>
            </section>

        </article>
    </div>
</main>

<script>
    (function () {
        var links = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#toc .toc-link'));
        var sections = links.map(function (a) { return document.getElementById(a.getAttribute('href').slice(1)); });

        function update() {
            var current = 0;
            var atBottom = window.innerHeight + window.scrollY >= document.documentElement.scrollHeight - 4;
            if (atBottom) {
                current = sections.length - 1;
            } else {
                sections.forEach(function (sec, i) {
                    if (sec && sec.getBoundingClientRect().top <= 140) current = i;
                });
            }
            links.forEach(function (a, i) { a.classList.toggle('is-active', i === current); });
        }

        window.addEventListener('scroll', update, { passive: true });
        window.addEventListener('resize', update);
        update();
    })();
</script>
